<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69657" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναιετάω</span></b> , in pres. forms, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άω</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Od.
			9.23
		</span></i>, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άει</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Hes.
			<u>Th.</u>
			775
		</span></i>, -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άουσι</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			4.45
		</span></i>; freq. in part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναιετάων</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			6.245
		</span></i>, al., acc. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άοντα</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			4.96
		</span></i>, etc., fem. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άωσα</span>
		(v.l. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άουσα</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.648
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			3.387
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			6.415
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			1.404
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			8.574
		</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όωσα</span> Aristarch.ad <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			6.415
		</span></i>): 
			Ion.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναιετάασκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.841
				</span></i>
			, etc.: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναίω</span>): </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of persons, <i>dwell</i>, freq. in 
				Ep.
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὶ ἐπὶ χθονὶ ναιετ άουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.153
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				564
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾗ ἔνι ναιετάασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.385
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. loci, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λακεδαίμονι ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.387
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρήτῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.523
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ χθονί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					621
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ ὅροις, ἀμφὶ . . θέμεθλα
				ναιετάοντες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				4.180
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.acc. loci,
				<i>dwell in, inhabit</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάρισαν,
				Ἰθάκην</span>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.841
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.21
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					816
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of places,
				<i>to be situated, lie</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.23
			</span></i>; of buildings, <i><span class="en">
				2.400
			</span></i>, al.: hence, <i>exist</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰθάκης ἔτι ναιεταούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.404
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 and Lyr. word, once in Trag., in part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναιετῶν</span> cj. Dind. metri gr. in
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1123
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
